Original commit body from 7ddaa8b6a527c751f5510e88a84e4d232292a3dd:

hypergumbo has been BROKEN ON PYTHON 3.10 -- its own declared minimum -- by one
unguarded import, and the matrix leg that said so was structurally unreadable.

`tomllib` entered the standard library in 3.11. Every package here declares
`requires-python = ">=3.10"`. user_config.py carried a bare top-level
`import tomllib`, and that module is imported broadly enough that the failure was
not graceful: the 2026-08-29 nightly py3.10 leg recorded

    ModuleNotFoundError: No module named 'tomllib'
    = 2905 failed, 18111 passed, 19 skipped, 1 xfailed, 124 errors in 1126.39s =

IT WAS THE ONLY UNGUARDED SITE IN THE TREE, which is why this ships a gate and
not just a patch. profile.py, linkers/subprocess_cli.py, py_deps.py and
scripts/generate-architecture ALL already carry
`try: import tomllib / except ImportError: import tomli as tomllib` and comment
it as the py3.10 path. Four authors followed the pattern, one did not, and
nothing checked.

THE BACKPORT WAS DECLARED NOWHERE, so even the four correct sites were not
actually working on 3.10 -- their fallback resolved to nothing and they degraded
silently (returning None) instead of parsing. `tomli~=2.0; python_version <
"3.11"` is now a real dependency of hypergumbo-core and
hypergumbo-lang-mainstream, the two packages that import tomllib.

THE GATE. tests/test_stdlib_version_guarded_imports.py walks 417 production
sources (including 78 scripts/ entries) and fails on any import of a stdlib
module whose debut is ABOVE the declared requires-python floor unless it sits
inside a `try` catching ImportError. The watched set is DERIVED from that floor,
read out of the pyproject files, so raising the floor to 3.11 retires tomllib
from the table on the commit that raises it.

VERIFIED BY REVERTING, not assumed: restored to the pre-fix shape the gate fails
naming user_config.py:43; it passes on the repaired tree. Three further controls
because a gate that never fires proves nothing:
  * the watched set must be NON-EMPTY for the current floor -- a floor above
    every entry would turn the main assertion into a green tick over nothing;
  * the four files that genuinely import tomllib are named, so the AST walker is
    demonstrably reaching real imports rather than finding none;
  * a package importing tomllib must DECLARE the backport, since a guard whose
    fallback is undeclared still fails on the floor.

The scripts/ half of that walk nearly covered nothing: the first cut wrote
`A and B and C or D`, which binds as `(A and B and C) or D` and excluded every
shebanged file -- i.e. exactly the python scripts it meant to add. The shebang is
now read rather than used to exclude, and generate-architecture is in scope.

THIS IS WHAT INV-bozid'S MASKING WAS HIDING. The py3.10 leg is one of four in a
matrix whose verdict Woodpecker collapses into a single aggregate commit status,
attached to whatever commit was dev's tip at 05:30 -- never HEAD by the time
anyone looks. `ci-debug cron-status`, added for that item in the preceding
change, surfaced the red leg on its first run; `ci-debug status` reported nothing
about it.

